  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1004 PM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nWhat barely qualifies as a cold front will approach Middle TN\novernight Thursday into Friday morning, bringing a broad swath of\nshowers and the occasional thunderstorm. The main areas of higher\nPoPs (>60%) will be confined north of I-40 since this front is\nexpected to promptly stall out Friday morning and slowly lift \nback north as a warm front over the weekend. This pattern will \nkeep PoPs above 50% each afternoon through the weekend, along with\ngrossly above normal temperatures in the 90s. Unfortunately, no \nclear relief is in sight. LREF mean 500 mb heights place another \nhighly amplified midlevel ridge over the southeastern CONUS again\nnext week.",
